'' THIS is a POINTER to the owning type and a real parameter, which is what fbc's own C
'' says: 'struct $1T* THIS$1'. Without the type 'this.v' did not type; without the
'' parameter '@this' named an uninitialised local while every call site dutifully passed
'' a receiver into nothing.
''
'' Every way of naming a receiver has to reach the same place: written 'this', a dot on a
'' value, a dot on a deref, an arrow, a chained call, and an UNQUALIFIED sibling call
'' with no base written at all.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/this.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: func void _ZN1T6CALLEREv(ptr $0)
'' EXPECT-OUT: store @this, $0
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN1T1MEv(@@obj)
'' EXPECT-NOT: call void _ZN1T1MEv()
